{"_meta":{"as_of":"2026-11-10T15:15:08+00:00","coverage":"10/10","note":"Earnings dates and consensus from Yahoo Finance \u2014 often estimated rather than company-confirmed, so treat them as approximate until close. Policy and catalyst entries are hand-dated in the research files."},"events":[{"d":"2026-07-28","type":"policy","t":"LIVE \u2014 FCC Covered List now bars foreign-produced robots (Jul 28, 2026)","why":"Adopted, not proposed. Any ground-moving device over 4.4lb (with dock) that senses, connects and navigates cannot get FCC equipment authorisation unless the Department of War grants a Conditional Approval. Read the carve-outs before pricing it: industrial robotic ARMS, medical robots, vehicles and drones are explicitly excluded, so Fanuc, Yaskawa, ABB, KUKA/Midea, Estun and Doosan's cobots are untouched. What is caught is humanoids, quadrupeds and autonomous mobile robots \u2014 9880.HK UBTech head-on, 277810.KQ Rainbow Robotics and TER's MiR unit on the same terms despite being allied, plus 1810.HK Xiaomi's consumer line. HSAI is hit second-hand through its customers' US market access. The asymmetry is the point: US-produced humanoids get a market cleared by rule, everyone else queues for a discretionary exemption.","hits":"act, sen"},{"d":"2026-08-04","type":"policy","t":"Chinese WFE tools qualifying at Samsung and SK Hynix","why":"Reuters, Aug 4 2026: both Korean memory makers have been testing AMEC etch tools for their China fabs \u2014 begun ~2 years ago, aimed at SERVICING and upgrading existing lines rather than adding capacity, after Washington revoked their validated-end-user status in 2025 and replaced it with an annual licence. Small in units, large in meaning: qualification is the slow half of the WFE moat, and it is being done by the two customers whose sign-off other buyers copy. Deutsche Bank has NAURA, AMEC, Piotech and ACM Research each clearing $1B of revenue in 2026 and together taking 25-30% of China's ~$28B WFE market. This is the external bear case (see Thesis) arriving as an event rather than an opinion \u2014 watch whether qualification stays confined to China fabs.","hits":"wfe"},{"d":"2026-09-30","type":"catalyst","t":"800-volt DC racks \u2014 first volume shipments","why":"Opens the SiC/GaN power-chip story: Infineon, onsemi, Navitas, Delta, Lite-On.","hits":"Power & Cooling"},{"d":"2026-09-30","type":"catalyst","t":"Unitree IPO prices on the STAR board","why":"The first real public-market test of humanoid-maker economics.","hits":"Humanoid Robotics"},{"d":"2026-10-15","type":"catalyst","t":"TSMC Q3 report \u2014 does capex fear break?","why":"The best sentiment gauge for the whole AI supply chain \u2014 and the catalyst on our #1 entry window.","hits":"Foundry & Packaging"},{"d":"2026-10-27","type":"catalyst","t":"SK Hynix Q3: delayed HBM4 revenue lands","why":"The catalyst on our #2 entry window: confirms or breaks the 'repriced, not broken' read.","hits":"Memory (HBM)"},{"d":"2026-11-02","type":"earnings","tk":"AEHR","n":"Aehr Test Systems","conv":2,"froth":3,"eps":0.13,"eps_lo":0.12,"eps_hi":0.13,"dd":-58.9,"ts":1793653200,"when":"post","xt":"16:00 EST","rep":{"act":0.28,"est":0.13,"when":"2026-11-02","surp":121.0,"move":11.65,"live":true,"post":1.71}},{"d":"2026-11-02","type":"earnings","tk":"AEIS","n":"Advanced Energy Industries","conv":2,"froth":2,"eps":3.04,"eps_lo":3.0,"eps_hi":3.27,"dd":-43.6,"ts":1793653200,"when":"post","xt":"16:00 EST","rep":{"act":3.65,"est":3.04,"when":"2026-11-02","surp":19.9,"move":11.31,"live":true,"post":0.32}},{"d":"2026-11-02","type":"earnings","tk":"ICHR","n":"Ichor Holdings","conv":1,"froth":2,"eps":0.45,"eps_lo":0.45,"eps_hi":0.47,"dd":-69.3,"ts":1793653200,"when":"post","xt":"16:00 EST","rep":{"act":0.63,"est":0.45,"when":"2026-11-02","surp":38.8,"move":11.25,"live":true,"post":0.44}},{"d":"2026-11-02","type":"earnings","tk":"ON","n":"onsemi","conv":2,"froth":1,"eps":1.01,"eps_lo":0.85,"eps_hi":0.93,"dd":-48.4,"ts":1793653200,"when":"post","xt":"16